---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Workflows & context"
  description="Carry evidence through a caller-driven investigation, ask for a final expert opinion, or compare independent participants."
  toc={[
    ["steps", "Run an investigation"],
    ["replay", "Continue a conversation"],
    ["context", "Attach evidence"],
    ["consensus", "Consult several participants"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="steps">Run an investigation</h2>
  <p>
    Choose a <a href="/mcp/tools/#workflow">guided investigation</a>. Send a
    step and the findings you already have. Investigate in your own client
    between calls. The last step may invoke an advisory expert according to that
    tool’s validation and confidence settings. Set{" "}
    <code>use_assistant_model: false</code> on each step to keep investigation
    with the caller.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP · debug · first step"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        step: "Reproduce the parser error with an empty record.",
        step_number: 1,
        total_steps: 2,
        next_step_required: true,
        findings: "A record with zero fields fails.",
        use_assistant_model: false,
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <p>
    Use the returned continuation ID, increment the step number, and supply the
    new evidence. Substitute the real ID in this example.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="MCP · debug · final step"
    code={JSON.stringify(
      {
        step: "Check whether a missing field reaches the parser.",
        step_number: 2,
        total_steps: 2,
        next_step_required: false,
        findings: "The fixture reproduced an unguarded first-field read.",
        continuation_id: "<returned continuation ID>",
        use_assistant_model: false,
      },
      null,
      2,
    )}
  />
  <p>
    <a href="/mcp/tools/planner/">planner</a>,{" "}
    <a href="/mcp/tools/docgen/">docgen</a> and{" "}
    <a href="/mcp/tools/tracer/">tracer</a> have self-contained workflows. They
    guide the host through planning, documentation and tracing.
  </p>
  <h2 id="replay">Continue a conversation</h2>
  <p>
    Capture the server-issued <code>continuation_id</code> and pass it to a
    compatible subsequent tool. The server replays bounded context and
    serializes updates for the ID. Defaults are three hours of inactivity, 50
    individual messages and 128 KiB of replay. A response can report pruned
    history. After expiry or restart, start a new conversation with a summary of
    the evidence you need.
  </p>
  <p>
    A repeated workflow transition with the same inputs can return its cached
    result. Changing an already-recorded transition can return{" "}
    <code>workflow_conflict</code>. Native CLI sessions use{" "}
    <a href="/mcp/native-tasks/">task handles</a>.
  </p>
  <h2 id="context">Attach evidence</h2>
  <p>
    Use absolute paths under the chosen client’s approved roots. Select
    individual regular text files. Tools use <code>absolute_file_paths</code> or{" "}
    <code>relevant_files</code> as shown in their schemas. The verified Codex
    consultation profile accepts explicit local PNG, JPEG, GIF and WebP image
    paths. Put the image paths in <code>images</code>. Native tasks reject image
    input.
  </p>
  <p>
    Clink checks up to 256 declared files and images and 64 MiB of source
    context. Assembled inline prompts are bounded at 1 MiB. Supply a narrower
    excerpt when required evidence is too large. A declared{" "}
    <code>prompt.txt</code> can provide the primary prompt for supported simple
    tools and counts toward the bounds.
  </p>
  <h2 id="consensus">Consult several participants</h2>
  <p>
    Start with two to eight entries in <code>models</code>. Choose participants
    by client, role, model and stance. Participants receive independent inputs
    and the caller owns synthesis. The default sequential mode advances through
    caller steps. Set <code>execution_mode: "parallel"</code> to gather outcomes
    in input order under the shared process limit.
  </p>
  <p>
    Check every result and retain any individual errors. Clink compares a
    bounded manifest of declared files around consultation. Changed files
    invalidate comparison. This check does not freeze a working tree.{" "}
    <a href="/mcp/tools/consensus/#example">Copy a two-participant example</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
